The forecasting pipeline developed during this internship produces forecasts at multiple aggregation levels and for several forecasting models. Exploring these outputs through static figures alone rapidly becomes impractical due to the number of possible combinations between deposit centers, destination countries, forecasting horizons, and candidate models.

To facilitate forecast exploration and comparison, an interactive visualization layer was implemented using Altair@altair. This component allows users to dynamically navigate reconciled forecasts and historical observations through an intuitive filtering interface.

=== Altair Dashboard Architecture

The visualization system is designed as the final layer of the forecasting pipeline. It consumes reconciled forecasts together with historical observations and exposes an interactive interface enabling users to explore different hierarchical levels.

The overall architecture is illustrated in @fig-dashboard-architecture.

